worker_module_budget
  module "formal_ai_worker_calendar_and_proofs.js"
  ceiling 1208
  rationale "Proof requests, weekday reasoning, calendar event creation with its ICS and Google Calendar links, and concept rendering. Issue #658 cut this module out of one oversized worker file by line count; R1188-U5 named it after what it holds. Its ceiling falls as its logic moves into js/wasm-worker. Ceiling moved 1264 to 1294 with the canonical operand order and entity-grounded hours mirror arms. Ceiling moved 1294 to 1311 for the calendar offset hook (calendar_reasoning: N days/weeks after/before a weekday). Ceiling moved 1311 to 1314 for the month-offset hook (calendar_reasoning: N months after/before a month or weekday). Ceiling moved 1314 to 1317 for the date-weekday hook (calendar_reasoning: the weekday a stated date falls on, R1017). Ceiling 1319 (2026-10-07, #1175 routing probes): a named weekday is a date signal for the calendar-create gate, twin of calendar_create.rs mentions_calendar_create_request. Ceiling lowered 1319 to 1206 for the issue #918 calendar batch (2026-10-08): the weekday name table, the cue arrays of the event parser and the relation, current-day and confirmation templates moved to the calendar_* tables of data/seed/handler-rules.lino and seeded responses. Ceiling moved 1206 to 1208 (R1188-U5): the first comment lines say what the module holds."
